# Source-derived semantics

- The source contains one instruction paragraph followed by one empty div with a 200px by 200px content box.
- The tested declaration is background: repeat-x bottom green scroll; and is preserved verbatim because its token order and valid shorthand parsing are the assertion.
- With no image, repeat, position, and attachment are visually inert; the required green fill is an observable all-or-nothing parser oracle.

# Compatibility adjustments

- Visible text uses one wrapping outer text with nested bold text and ordinary U+0020; the test box uses a class-scoped view.
- Content-box sizing and explicit body/paragraph spacing reproduce Web setup without relying on Lynx margin collapse.
- No tested background component is split, removed, or replaced.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- Lynx documents background and the color/repeat/position components, while background-attachment is unsupported.
- This card keeps scroll under test and remains pending; a missing green square is a valid engine failure, not an adapter skip.
